{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "orders",
      "label": "Orders",
      "role": "producer",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "ci",
      "label": "buf / registry",
      "role": "registry",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "queue",
      "label": "Queue (2 days)",
      "role": "broker",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "billing",
      "label": "Billing",
      "role": "consumer",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shipping",
      "label": "Shipping",
      "role": "consumer",
      "x": 82,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "analytics",
      "label": "Analytics",
      "role": "consumer",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 86
    }
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "Order event v1 has id=1, amount_cents=2, status=3, discount_cents=4. Orders writes it to the queue, which keeps 2 days of events. Billing, Shipping and Analytics all read v1.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "order v1"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "billing",
          "label": "v1"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "shipping",
          "label": "v1"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "orders": "writes v1",
        "billing": "reads v1",
        "shipping": "reads v1",
        "analytics": "reads v1 (JSON)"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "Orders adds currency as new field 5, optional, and deploys first. The check passes BACKWARD and FORWARD. Billing is still on v1: it sees an unknown tag 5, skips it, and carries on. That is forward compatibility.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "ci",
          "to": "orders",
          "label": "FULL ok"
        },
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "v2 +currency"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "billing",
          "label": "skips 5"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "ci": "add field 5: pass",
        "orders": "writes v2",
        "billing": "v1, ignores 5"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "billing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Shipping deploys v2 and reads the 2 days of old v1 events still queued. They have no field 5, so currency reads as empty. That is backward compatibility, and why a new reader has to survive old data.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "shipping",
          "label": "old v1 event"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "shipping": "v2, currency empty",
        "queue": "v1 and v2 mixed"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "shipping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Someone renames amount_cents to total_cents. On the protobuf wire this is invisible: the number is still 2, so Billing and Shipping are fine. But Analytics reads a JSON export keyed by name and cannot find amount_cents.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "total_cents"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "analytics",
          "label": "JSON"
        },
        {
          "from": "analytics",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "crash"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "billing": "ok (field 2)",
        "shipping": "ok (field 2)",
        "analytics": "missing key: crash"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "analytics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The safe way is expand and contract: Orders writes both names for a 30 day window, Analytics moves to total_cents, then the old name stops and is reserved. Three small compatible releases instead of one break.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "both names"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "analytics",
          "label": "ok"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "orders": "dual-write 30 d",
        "analytics": "migrated",
        "ci": "FULL ok"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "Next, discount_cents (field 4) is removed. Billing still on v1 now reads discount 0 instead of 500 cents: no error, it simply bills the full price. Stop readers from using a field before writers drop it.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "no field 4"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "billing",
          "label": "discount = 0"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "billing": "silent default",
        "orders": "drops field 4"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "billing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "A new developer adds tip_cents and, seeing 4 is free, reuses it. The queue still holds old events with discount 500 in field 4. Shipping reads that as tip_cents=500: same wire type, no error, wrong value.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "shipping",
          "label": "4 = 500"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "shipping": "tip = 500 (wrong)",
        "queue": "old events, field 4"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "shipping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "In CI, buf breaking rejects the pull request (field 4 deleted without being reserved), and a registry in FULL_TRANSITIVE mode checks every earlier version. tip_cents gets field 6 and the bug never ships.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "orders",
          "to": "ci",
          "label": "PR: tip_cents=4"
        },
        {
          "from": "ci",
          "to": "orders",
          "label": "rejected"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "ci": "4 not reserved: fail",
        "orders": "use field 6"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "ci"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
